---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import AffiliateDisclosure from '../../components/AffiliateDisclosure.astro';
import { affiliates } from '../../data/affiliates';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Surfer SEO Alternatives: Frase, Writesonic & More"
  description="Compare Frase, Writesonic, and Semrush content tools as Surfer SEO alternatives—when each fits a budget content team. Updated Aug 2026."
  moneyPage
>
  <AffiliateDisclosure />
  <article class="prose-spl mt-6 max-w-3xl">
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">August 12, 2026 · Research comparison</p>
    <h1 class="!mt-2 text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900">Best Surfer SEO Alternatives for Content Teams on a Budget</h1>
    <p>
      <a href={affiliates.surfer.url} rel="nofollow sponsored noopener" target="_blank">Surfer SEO</a>
      is a popular on-page content optimizer, but its price can feel heavy for early-stage teams. This guide covers
      practical alternatives—especially
      <a href={affiliates.frase.url} rel="nofollow sponsored noopener" target="_blank">Frase</a>,
      <a href={affiliates.writesonic.url} rel="nofollow sponsored noopener" target="_blank">Writesonic</a>, and
      using <a href={affiliates.semrush.url} rel="nofollow sponsored noopener" target="_blank">Semrush</a>
      content tools only if you already need the suite.
    </p>

    <div class="not-prose my-6 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900">Quick pick</p>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600">
        Briefs + optimize on a budget → Frase. Draft + light SEO in one seat → Writesonic. Already on Semrush → use its content tools before adding Surfer.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href={affiliates.frase.url} class="btn-primary" rel="nofollow sponsored noopener" target="_blank">Check Frase pricing</a>
        <a href={affiliates.writesonic.url} class="btn-secondary" rel="nofollow sponsored noopener" target="_blank">Check Writesonic</a>
        <a href="/compare/surfer-seo-alternatives" class="btn-secondary">Compare cards →</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>What “alternative” should mean</h2>
    <p>
      A real Surfer alternative should help writers brief and/or score content against SERP patterns.
      A cheaper AI writer alone is not a substitute unless it includes usable optimization guidance.
    </p>

    <h2>Frase</h2>
    <p>
      Frase is frequently chosen for SERP-driven briefs and optimization at a lower entry cost than Surfer for many plans.
      Best when your bottleneck is briefing and coverage, not enterprise NLP theater.
    </p>

    <h2>Writesonic</h2>
    <p>
      If you currently pay for a writer <em>and</em> Surfer, consolidating into Writesonic (or similar) can cut spend.
      Best when one person owns draft + optimize. Weaker when you need best-in-class SERP analysis depth.
    </p>

    <h2>Semrush content tools</h2>
    <p>
      Semrush is not a cheap Surfer clone. It becomes a sensible “alternative” only when keyword research, audits,
      and competitive intel are already on your shopping list. Buying Semrush solely to replace Surfer is usually the wrong savings move.
    </p>

    <h2>Budget recommendation</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Need briefs + optimize on a budget → try Frase first.</li>
      <li>Need generation + light SEO together → consider Writesonic.</li>
      <li>Already paying for Semrush → use its content features before adding Surfer.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      <strong>Related reading:</strong> <a href="/compare/frase-vs-surfer">Frase vs Surfer</a>, <a href="/compare/semrush-vs-surfer-seo">Semrush vs Surfer</a>, <a href="/blog/ai-content-ops-stack-research-draft-optimize">content ops stack</a>, and <a href="/compare/semrush-vs-ahrefs-vs-free">Semrush vs Ahrefs vs free</a> for research-suite decisions.
    </p>
    <p>
      Card-level Best for / Skip if: <a href="/compare/surfer-seo-alternatives">Surfer alternatives comparison</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
